From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 13:10:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 14/22] s: tell Poseidon about a host controller that is present

PsdStackLoader starts the stack and restores saved preferences. A machine
that has never had Poseidon configured has no hardware in those, so the
stack comes up with nothing attached and no USB device is ever seen.

Guarded on the device file existing, so it is inert anywhere the driver is
not installed.
---
 workbench/s/Startup-Sequence | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/workbench/s/Startup-Sequence b/workbench/s/Startup-Sequence
index 1a5b9fffb1..8a2aef5f81 100644
--- a/workbench/s/Startup-Sequence
+++ b/workbench/s/Startup-Sequence
@@ -105,6 +105,15 @@
 If EXISTS "C:PsdStackLoader"
     PsdStackLoader >NIL:
 EndIf
+; A host controller in DEVS:USBHardware is not found by itself: PsdStackLoader
+; starts the stack and restores saved preferences, but a machine that has never
+; had Poseidon configured has no hardware in them. Tell it about the controller
+; that is actually present, if one is.
+If EXISTS "DEVS:USBHardware/usb2otg.device"
+    Echo "starting AddUSBHardware" >"SDCARD0P0:usb-hardware.log"
+    AddUSBHardware DEVS:USBHardware/usb2otg.device >>"SDCARD0P0:usb-hardware.log"
+    Echo "finished AddUSBHardware" >>"SDCARD0P0:usb-hardware.log"
+EndIf
 If EXISTS "C:BTStackLoader"
     BTStackLoader >NIL:
 EndIf
